      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION SE/WP/72.14\n\nINTER-COUNTRY SEMINAR ON\nSURVEILLANCE IN SMALLPOX ERADICATION INDEXED\n\nNew Delhi, 30 October - 2 November 1972\n\nCONTROL OF SMALLPOX\nIN DELHI MUNICIPAL CORPORATION\n\nby\n\nDr P. H. Jeswani?\n\n1. Introduction\nUnion Territory of Delhi has three administrative units:\n\ni) Delhi Municipal Corporation (population 37.6 lacs.)\nii) New Delhi Municipal Committee (population 2.96 lacs.)\n\niii) Delhi Cantonment Board (population 0.85 lacs.)\n\nDelhi Municipal Corporation looks after the implementation of NSEP in\nthe entire Union Territory of Delhi excluding NDMC, the Cantonm",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The first page of a 1972 seminar paper on controlling smallpox in the Delhi Municipal Corporation, describing the administrative units of Delhi and the corporation's role in the national eradication programme. It outlines the organisation of the eradication work in the city.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
