      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SE/WP/72.14\npage 2\n\nactivities could be pursued.\n\nFurther, there is an I.D. Hospital, which receives cases of smallpox\nfrom the neighbouring districts.\n\nThere are 138 vaccinators, i.e. one vaccinator per 25 000 population.\nEach vaccinator has been provided with a recognition card and a map of his\nassigned area. He is required to vaccinate the population from door to door,\nand to vaccinate the newborns in maternity and nursing homes in his area.\nHis principal function of course is to be on the ‘hunt' to detect any case\nof 'fever with rash' and report immediately by telephone to his supervisors.",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes Delhi's smallpox control staff and structures, including 138 door-to-door vaccinators who also search for fever with rash, and 55 birth, death and vaccination centres that act as reporting points. It notes the use of bifurcated needles and freeze-dried vaccine, giving near-complete success in primary vaccination, though only 60–70% of vaccinations are inspected.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
