      "target": "../sections/page-004.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SE/WP/72.14\npage 4\n\nThe majority of cases, however, were reported from the following\nzones :-\n\nShahdara Zone (7 outbreaks, 25 cases)\n\nRural Zone (11 outbreaks, 19 cases)\n\nKarol Bagh Zone (7 outbreaks, 17 cases)\nSadar Pahar Ganj Zone (5 outbreaks, 14 cases)\nCity Zone (6 outbreaks, 10 cases)\n\nNew Delhi South Zone (7 outbreaks, 9 cases)\nIn the remaining two zones, the position is as follows:-\n\nCivil Line Zone (3 outbreaks, 4 cases) and\n\nWest Zone (2 outbreaks, 2 cases).\n\nIn all, 53 areas in 8 zones were affected, resulting in 100 cases. In\n30 instances, the source of infection was traced to the n",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Lists the 1972 smallpox outbreaks and cases by zone in Delhi, totalling 100 cases in 53 areas, and traces many sources of infection to neighbouring states such as Uttar Pradesh and Haryana. It criticises vague source reporting and stresses the need for proper epidemiological investigation, given the many single-case outbreaks.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
