      "target": "../sections/page-005.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "SE/WP/72.14\npage 5\n\nThe recently introduced weekly smallpox epidemic reporting system has\nbeen established. Ail the 32 Vaccination Inspectors have been instructed to\nsubmit weekly smallpox epidemic reports of their areas regularly, and in time.\nEven 'NIL' reports are being insisted upon. The Medical Superintendent of\n\nthe 1.D. Hospital, Delhi, is contacted by telephone daily regarding any\nadmission of a smallpox case. — :\n\nACKNOWLEDGEMENT\n\nI am deeply grateful to Lt. Col. 0. N. Tyagi, Municipal Health Officer,\nDelhi for permitting me to participate in the Seminar. His keen interest\nin the prog",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes a new weekly smallpox reporting system in Delhi, with nil reports required and daily checks with the infectious diseases hospital, and closes with the author's acknowledgements.",
